; Puzzle rooms: examples of the puzzle things (puzzles.py, the editor's round B2, approved 31 October 2026).
; Each is a side room with a find behind bars or water; the way on never hangs on one. A room with blocks has a
; lever that sets it back as drawn. The format: README.txt.

; ================================================================== plates and blocks
NAME:   weighing hall
SHAPE:  a hall with plates in the floor
DEPTH:  1
WEIGHT: 4
MOOD:   Two worn plates are set in the floor, and two blocks of stone stand near them. Behind bars, a chest.
MOOD:   A weighing hall. The plates in the floor sit a finger proud, waiting for a load.
THING:  P = pressure plate do:pressure
THING:  B = stone block do:block
THING:  Q = bars
THING:  R = lever do:lever
COUNTER: plates 0
EVENT:  when=press at=P then=add:plates again=yes
EVENT:  when=release at=P then=sub:plates again=yes
EVENT:  when=count:plates:2 then=open:Q then=msg:"Both plates are down. With a long grinding, the bars sink into the floor."
EVENT:  when=bump at=R then=reset then=msg:"Chains rattle in the walls: the blocks are hauled back where they stood." again=yes
MAP
      c
      Q
 ...........
 ...........
 ...B...B...
 ...........
 ...P...P...
 ...........
 R..........
      +
ENDMAP

; ================================================================== braziers
NAME:   brazier hall
SHAPE:  a hall of fire bowls
DEPTH:  1
WEIGHT: 4
MOOD:   One brazier burns. Three stand cold, full of old pitch. Behind bars, something glints.
MOOD:   A hall of fire bowls, all but one gone cold. The bars across the far alcove are black with soot.
THING:  F = fire bowl do:brazier
THING:  O = cold fire bowl do:brazier
THING:  Q = bars
COUNTER: fires 0
EVENT:  when=lit at=O then=add:fires again=yes
EVENT:  when=count:fires:3 then=open:Q then=msg:"The last brazier roars up. The bars glow red, and draw back into the stone."
MAP
     c
     Q
 .........
 .O.....O.
 .........
 ....F....
 .........
 .O.......
 .........
     +
ENDMAP

; ================================================================== mirrors and the sun
NAME:   mirror hall
SHAPE:  a hall with a shaft of daylight
DEPTH:  2
WEIGHT: 4
MOOD:   Daylight falls in through a shaft in the roof. Mirrors stand on swivels, and a golden disc waits in the dark.
MOOD:   A hall of mirrors and one shaft of sun. Someone built this to carry the light.
THING:  S = shaft of daylight do:shaft
THING:  M = mirror on a swivel do:swivel
THING:  D = sun disc do:sundisc
THING:  Q = bars
EVENT:  when=sun at=D then=open:Q then=msg:"Light pours off the disc. The bars on the alcove slide up into the roof."
MAP
   S     c
 ........Q..
 ...........
 ...........
 ..M.....M..
 ...........
 ...........
 ........D..
 ...........
      +
ENDMAP

; ================================================================== crystal switches
NAME:   crystal vault
SHAPE:  a vault of red and blue blocks
DEPTH:  2
WEIGHT: 4
MOOD:   A crystal hums on a stand. Red blocks shut an alcove; blue ones lie sunk in the floor.
MOOD:   Red and blue stone, set in the floor like a game. A crystal glows red in the middle.
THING:  X = red crystal switch do:crystal
THING:  E = red block
THING:  U = sunk blue block
MAP
     c
     E
 .........
 ..U.U.U..
 .........
 ....X....
 .........
     +
ENDMAP

; ================================================================== bells in order
NAME:   bell chamber
SHAPE:  a chamber of three bells
DEPTH:  1
WEIGHT: 4
MOOD:   Three bells hang in a row. Behind bars, a chest. Notches are cut in the stone under each bell.
MOOD:   A bell chamber. The ropes are long gone; you would have to strike them by hand.
THING:  A = bell do:bell
THING:  B = bell do:bell
THING:  C = bell do:bell
THING:  Q = bars
EVENT:  when=bump at=C then=msg:"Under this bell, one notch is cut." again=yes
EVENT:  when=bump at=A then=msg:"Under this bell, two notches are cut." again=yes
EVENT:  when=bump at=B then=msg:"Under this bell, three notches are cut." again=yes
EVENT:  when=order:CAB then=open:Q then=msg:"The last note hangs in the air. The bars lift away."
MAP
     c
     Q
 .........
 .A..B..C.
 .........
 .........
     +
ENDMAP

; ================================================================== water and the sluice
NAME:   flooded cellar
SHAPE:  a cellar under water
DEPTH:  2
WEIGHT: 4
MOOD:   A flooded cellar. Something lies on a dry stone in the middle, out of reach. A sluice gate is set in the wall.
MOOD:   Dark water fills the cellar. A rusted sluice gate stands shut.
THING:  G = sluice gate do:sluice
MAP
       G
 .............
 .~~~~~~~~~~~.
 .~~~~,,,~~~~.
 .~~~~,c,~~~~.
 .~~~~,,,~~~~.
 .~~~~~~~~~~~.
 .............
       +
ENDMAP

; ================================================================== the riddle stone
NAME:   riddle stone
SHAPE:  a hall with a lettered stone
DEPTH:  1
WEIGHT: 4
MOOD:   A tall stone stands before a barred alcove, cut deep with letters.
MOOD:   A riddle stone. The old builders liked their games.
THING:  T = riddle stone do:riddle
THING:  Q = bars
EVENT:  when=solved at=T then=open:Q
MAP
     c
     Q
 .........
 .........
 ....T....
 .........
     +
ENDMAP

; ================================================================== the keyhole
NAME:   key vault
SHAPE:  a vault with a keyhole
DEPTH:  2
WEIGHT: 4
MOOD:   A keyhole is set in the stone beside a barred alcove. Its key must lie somewhere in this place.
THING:  K = keyhole do:keyhole
THING:  Q = bars
EVENT:  when=unlock at=K then=open:Q
MAP
     c
 K   Q
 .........
 .........
 .........
     +
ENDMAP

; ================================================================== the idol
NAME:   idol shrine
SHAPE:  a shrine with a golden idol
DEPTH:  3
WEIGHT: 3
MOOD:   A golden idol stands alone on a plinth. The ceiling above it is cracked.
MOOD:   A small shrine, and a god of gold on a plinth. Too easy.
THING:  I = golden idol on a plinth do:idol
THING:  Z = sarcophagus do:sarcophagus
MAP
 ...........
 .Z.......Z.
 ...........
 .....I.....
 ...........
 .Z.......Z.
 ...........
      +
ENDMAP

; ================================================================== ice
NAME:   ice hall
SHAPE:  a hall floored with ice
DEPTH:  2
WEIGHT: 4
MOOD:   The floor is ice, smooth as glass. On the far side, a chest.
MOOD:   Frost on every wall, and ice underfoot. Once you start, you will not stop until something stops you.
THING:  I = slick ice do:ice
MAP
 ..c..
 .....
 IIIII
 II#II
 IIIII
 IIIII
 #IIII
 .....
   +
ENDMAP

; ================================================================== spikes
NAME:   spike walk
SHAPE:  a walk of spike holes
DEPTH:  2
WEIGHT: 4
MOOD:   The floor is pocked with holes. As you watch, spikes drive up out of them, and sink back.
MOOD:   A walk of spike holes. They keep a rhythm; you could learn it.
THING:  Z = spike holes do:spikes
MAP
 ...c...
 .......
 ZZZZZZZ
 ZZZZZZZ
 ZZZZZZZ
 .......
    +
ENDMAP

; ================================================================== arrows
NAME:   arrow hall
SHAPE:  a hall with arrow slits
DEPTH:  2
WEIGHT: 3
MOOD:   Arrow slits line the walls. A plate lies in the middle of the floor, and a chest beyond it.
MOOD:   A hall of slits in the stone. Whoever guarded this did not need to be here.
THING:  P = pressure plate do:pressure
THING:  S = arrow slit
EVENT:  when=press at=P then=arrows:S again=yes
MAP
  .......
  ...c...
  .......
 S...P...S
  .......
  .......
     +
ENDMAP

; ================================================================== the crumbling bridge
NAME:   crumbling bridge
SHAPE:  a chasm with a bridge of old stone
DEPTH:  3
WEIGHT: 3
MOOD:   A chasm splits the room. A bridge of old stone crosses it, already crumbling. On the far side, a chest and a rope.
MOOD:   The bridge will bear you once. The rope on the far side goes down.
THING:  K = crumbling floor do:crumble
THING:  W = rope down do:rope
MAP
 ..c..W..
 ........
 vvvvKvvv
 vvvvKvvv
 ........
 ........
    +
ENDMAP

; ================================================================== the cracked wall
NAME:   cracked wall
SHAPE:  a hall with a cracked wall
DEPTH:  1
WEIGHT: 3
MOOD:   One wall of this hall is cracked right through. Cold air breathes out of the crack.
THING:  W = cracked wall do:cracked
MAP
 ....c....
 ....W....
 .........
 .........
     +
ENDMAP

; ================================================================== the old god's niche
NAME:   old gods niche
SHAPE:  a hall of an old god
DEPTH:  2
WEIGHT: 3
MOOD:   An old god's hall. An idol with gem eyes stares from its niche; a bowl of coins lies before it.
MOOD:   A shrine to a god no one names now. A still pool, a chained book, a stone coffin.
THING:  G = idol with gem eyes do:eyes
THING:  O = offering bowl do:offering
THING:  Y = scrying pool do:scrying
THING:  H = chained book do:book
THING:  Z = sarcophagus do:sarcophagus
MAP
     G
 .........
 ....O....
 .Y.....H.
 .........
 .Z.....Z.
 .........
     +
ENDMAP

; ================================================================== more puzzle things (round C)
NAME:   statue hall
SHAPE:  a hall of two mirror statues
DEPTH:  2
WEIGHT: 3
MOOD:   Two statues of travellers stand in this hall. As you step in, they step too: one with you, one against you.
MOOD:   Mirror statues. Two plates wait in the floor, and the statues seem to know it.
THING:  M = mirror statue do:mimic
THING:  N = mirror statue do:mimicx
THING:  P = pressure plate do:pressure
THING:  Q = bars
THING:  R = lever do:lever
COUNTER: plates 0
EVENT:  when=press at=P then=add:plates again=yes
EVENT:  when=release at=P then=sub:plates again=yes
EVENT:  when=count:plates:2 then=open:Q then=msg:"Both plates sink. The bars slide away into the floor."
EVENT:  when=bump at=R then=reset then=msg:"The statues grind back to where they stood." again=yes
MAP
       c
       Q
 .............
 .P.........P.
 .............
 ...M.....N...
 .............
 .............
 R............
       +
ENDMAP

NAME:   pale statue
SHAPE:  a hall of pillars and a pale statue
DEPTH:  3
WEIGHT: 3
MOOD:   A pale statue stands among the pillars, its hands over its face. You do not like turning your back on it.
MOOD:   Pillars, a plate in the floor, and a statue that is not where it was.
THING:  S = pale statue do:stalker
THING:  P = pressure plate do:pressure
THING:  Q = bars
EVENT:  when=press at=P then=open:Q then=msg:"Something heavy settles on the plate. The bars lift."
MAP
       c
       Q
 .............
 .S.#.....#...
 .............
 .....P.......
 .............
 ...#.....#...
 .............
       +
ENDMAP

